  "創業於元祿四年（1691 年），本館為日本現存最古老的木造湯宿建築，列為群馬縣重要文化財；大正浪漫風格的「元祿之湯」拱窗浴場亦是其標誌。跨過紅色慶雲橋望向本館的景色，相傳是《神隱少女》湯屋場景的靈感原型之一。午餐於館內享用，餐後可在本館迴廊與「浪漫隧道」散策留影。": "Founded in 1691 (the fourth year of the Genroku era), the Main Building is Japan's oldest surviving wooden hot-spring inn structure and a designated Important Cultural Property of Gunma Prefecture; its arched-window bathhouse, Genroku-no-Yu, embodies the romantic spirit of the Taisho era and remains one of the property's most iconic features. The view of the Main Building across the red Keiun Bridge is said to be one of the inspirations for the bathhouse in Spirited Away. Lunch is enjoyed within the building, followed by a stroll for photographs along the Main Building's corridor and the \"Romance Tunnel.\"",
  "加濕器": "Humidifier",
